From: cvediver <cvediver@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Sep 2026 10:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: harden ML peer ID bookkeeping

Two hardening fixes for the host-side ML peer ID allocator, found
while root-causing the first-association downlink failure on the
GL-BE9300 (dead first TX burst; firmware TQM lost wakeup at
wal_tqm.c:866 / wal_tx_de_mgmt.c:879).

First, both remaining ML peer ID release sites clear the bitmap bit
unmasked and unbounded:

	if (!test_bit(ahsta->ml_peer_id, ah->quarantined_ml_peer_id_map))
		clear_bit(ahsta->ml_peer_id, ah->free_ml_peer_id_map);

in ath12k_mac_ml_station_remove() and at the ml_peer_id_clear error
label of ath12k_mac_op_sta_state(). This is the same defect class the
SSR path fix in ath12k_mac_dp_peer_cleanup() already addressed: a
value of ATH12K_MLO_PEER_ID_INVALID (0xFFFF, e.g. a double release) or
a composite id carrying ATH12K_PEER_ML_ID_VALID indexes kilobytes past
the ATH12K_MAX_MLO_PEERS-bit maps, corrupting the adjacent
ath12k_hw::dp_hw state (dp_peers[] RCU pointers) while leaking the
intended bit. Mask the id back to the host domain and bounds-check it
with a WARN_ON_ONCE before touching either bitmap, mirroring the SSR
fix. While here, make the release diagnostic truthful: it now prints
the masked host-domain id and whether the id was actually returned to
the pool or retained in quarantine.

Second, nothing clamps the usable ML peer ID count to the hardware
limit. ah->max_ml_peer_ids is seeded with the 1024-bit host bitmap
capacity and only reduced by the MLO setup complete v2 event. The
host, however, promises firmware hw_params->max_mlo_peer peers (256 on
these platforms) in both the QMI host capability request and the WMI
MLO setup path. If the v2 event is absent or lost, the round-robin
allocator will eventually hand firmware IDs beyond the promised range
- silently, with cross-chip peer mapping consequences entirely inside
firmware. Clamp the allocation bound to the smallest
hw_params->max_mlo_peer of the radios in the group at hw allocation
time; the setup complete event value can then only shrink it further.

Signed-off-by: cvediver <cvediver@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c | 41 +++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
index f791c2a..0865c61 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -7401,11 +7401,19 @@ static void ath12k_mac_ml_station_remove(struct ath12k_vif *ahvif,
 		ath12k_peer_ml_quarantine(ah, ahsta, ret);
 
 	if (sta->mlo) {
+		u16 ml_peer_id = ahsta->ml_peer_id & ~ATH12K_PEER_ML_ID_VALID;
+
-		ath12k_info(ath12k_ah_to_ar(ah, 0)->ab,
-			    "ml peer id %u freed for %pM\n",
-			    ahsta->ml_peer_id, sta->addr);
-		if (!test_bit(ahsta->ml_peer_id, ah->quarantined_ml_peer_id_map))
-			clear_bit(ahsta->ml_peer_id, ah->free_ml_peer_id_map);
+		if (!WARN_ON_ONCE(ml_peer_id >= ATH12K_MAX_MLO_PEERS)) {
+			bool quarantined =
+				test_bit(ml_peer_id,
+					 ah->quarantined_ml_peer_id_map);
+
+			ath12k_info(ath12k_ah_to_ar(ah, 0)->ab,
+				    "ml peer id %u released for %pM (quarantined=%d)\n",
+				    ml_peer_id, sta->addr, quarantined);
+			if (!quarantined)
+				clear_bit(ml_peer_id, ah->free_ml_peer_id_map);
+		}
 		ahsta->ml_peer_id = ATH12K_MLO_PEER_ID_INVALID;
 	}
 }
@@ -8127,11 +8127,19 @@ peer_delete:
 	ath12k_dp_peer_delete(&ah->dp_hw, sta->addr, sta);
 ml_peer_id_clear:
 	if (sta->mlo) {
+		u16 ml_peer_id = ahsta->ml_peer_id & ~ATH12K_PEER_ML_ID_VALID;
+
-		ath12k_info(ath12k_ah_to_ar(ah, 0)->ab,
-			    "ml peer id %u freed for %pM\n",
-			    ahsta->ml_peer_id, sta->addr);
-		if (!test_bit(ahsta->ml_peer_id, ah->quarantined_ml_peer_id_map))
-			clear_bit(ahsta->ml_peer_id, ah->free_ml_peer_id_map);
+		if (!WARN_ON_ONCE(ml_peer_id >= ATH12K_MAX_MLO_PEERS)) {
+			bool quarantined =
+				test_bit(ml_peer_id,
+					 ah->quarantined_ml_peer_id_map);
+
+			ath12k_info(ath12k_ah_to_ar(ah, 0)->ab,
+				    "ml peer id %u released for %pM (quarantined=%d)\n",
+				    ml_peer_id, sta->addr, quarantined);
+			if (!quarantined)
+				clear_bit(ml_peer_id, ah->free_ml_peer_id_map);
+		}
 		ahsta->ml_peer_id = ATH12K_MLO_PEER_ID_INVALID;
 	}
 exit:
@@ -15710,6 +15710,15 @@ static struct ath12k_hw *ath12k_mac_hw_allocate(struct ath12k_hw_group *ag,
 	ah->num_radio = num_pdev_map;
 	ah->max_ml_peer_ids = ATH12K_MAX_MLO_PEERS;
 
+	/* Never allocate ML peer IDs beyond what the weakest radio promised
+	 * to firmware (QMI host cap and WMI MLO setup both use
+	 * hw_params->max_mlo_peer); the MLO setup complete event value can
+	 * only shrink this further.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < num_pdev_map; i++)
+		ah->max_ml_peer_ids = min(ah->max_ml_peer_ids,
+					  pdev_map[i].ab->hw_params->max_mlo_peer);
+
 	mutex_init(&ah->hw_mutex);
 
 	spin_lock_init(&ah->survey_lock);
